        {
          "sentence": 26,
          "component": "HTML5 Server",
          "source": "one_call",
          "confidence": 1.0,
          "text": "Frontends receive other DDP events including method calls to send events to akka-apps."
        },
        {
          "sentence": 27,
          "component": "HTML5 Server",
          "source": "one_call",
          "confidence": 1.0,
          "text": "Frontends handle completely the Streamer redis events, i.e., Cursor, Annotations, External video share."
        },
        {
          "sentence": 28,
          "component": "HTML5 Server",
          "source": "one_call",
          "confidence": 1.0,
          "text": "Frontends still require MeetingStarted and MeetingEnded events to create/destroy per-meeting event processing queues."
        },
        {
          "sentence": 29,
          "component": "HTML5 Server",
          "source": "one_call",
          "confidence": 1.0,
          "text": "Backends handle all the non-streamer events."
        },
        {
          "sentence": 31,
          "component": "HTML5 Server",
          "source": "one_call",
          "confidence": 1.0,
          "text": "So individual backends only process redis events for the meetings matching the associated instanceId."
        },
        {
          "sentence": 32,
          "component": "HTML5 Server",
          "source": "one_call",
          "confidence": 1.0,
          "text": "ValidateAuthTokenResp is passed to backends as well, which is needed for the cases where you only have a backend, no fro"
        },
        {
          "sentence": 39,
          "component": "BBB web",
          "source": "one_call",
          "confidence": 1.0,
          "text": "The BigBlueButton API provides a third-party integration (such as the BigBlueButtonBN plugin for Moodle) with an endpoin"
        },
        {
          "sentence": 40,
          "component": "BBB web",
          "source": "one_call",
          "confidence": 1.0,
          "text": "Every access to BigBlueButton comes through a front-end portal (we refer to as a third-party application)."
        },
        {
          "sentence": 41,
          "component": "BBB web",
          "source": "one_call",
          "confidence": 1.0,
          "text": "BigBlueButton integrates Moodle, Wordpress, Canvas, Sakai, and others (see third-party integrations)."
        },
        {
          "sentence": 42,
          "component": "BBB web",
          "source": "one_call",
          "confidence": 1.0,
          "text": "BigBlueButton comes with its own front-end called Greenlight."
        },
        {
          "sentence": 43,
          "component": "BBB web",
          "source": "one_call",
          "confidence": 1.0,
          "text": "When using a learning management system (LMS) such as Moodle, teachers can setup BigBlueButton rooms within their course"
        },
        {
          "sentence": 44,
          "component": "BBB web",
          "source": "one_call",
          "confidence": 1.0,
          "text": "The BigBlueButton comes with some simple API demos."
        },
        {
          "sentence": 45,
          "component": "BBB web",
          "source": "one_call",
          "confidence": 1.0,
          "text": "Regardless of which front-end you use, they all use the API under the hood."
        },
        {
          "sentence": 55,
          "component": "Apps",
          "source": "one_call",
          "confidence": 1.0,
          "text": "The meeting business logic is in the MeetingActor."
        },
        {
          "sentence": 56,
          "component": "Apps",
          "source": "one_call",
          "confidence": 1.0,
          "text": "This is where information about the meeting is stored and where all messages for a meeting is processed."
        },
        {
          "sentence": 58,
          "component": "FSESL",
          "source": "one_call",
          "confidence": 1.0,
          "text": "We have extracted out the component that integrates with FreeSWITCH into it\u2019s own application."
        },
        {
          "sentence": 59,
          "component": "FSESL",
          "source": "one_call",
          "confidence": 1.0,
          "text": "This allows others who are using voice conference systems other than FreeSWITCH to easily create their own integration."
        },
        {
          "sentence": 64,
          "component": "FreeSWITCH",
          "source": "one_call",
          "confidence": 1.0,
          "text": "Users are able to join the voice conference through the headset."
        },
        {
          "sentence": 65,
          "component": "FreeSWITCH",
          "source": "one_call",
          "confidence": 1.0,
          "text": "Users joining through Google Chrome or Mozilla Firefox are able to take advantage of higher quality audio by connecting "
        },
        {
          "sentence": 76,
          "component": "Presentation Conversion",
          "source": "one_call",
          "confidence": 1.0,
          "text": "Uploaded presentations go through a conversion process in order to be displayed inside the client."
        },
        {
          "sentence": 77,
          "component": "Presentation Conversion",
          "source": "one_call",
          "confidence": 1.0,
          "text": "When the uploaded presentation is an Office document, it needs to be converted into PDF using LibreOffice."
        },
        {
          "sentence": 78,
          "component": "Presentation Conversion",
          "source": "one_call",
          "confidence": 1.0,
          "text": "The PDF document is then converted into scalable vector graphics (SVG) via bbb-web."
        },
        {
          "sentence": 79,
          "component": "Presentation Conversion",
          "source": "one_call",
          "confidence": 1.0,
          "text": "The conversion process sends progress messages to the client through the Redis pubsub."
        },
        {
          "sentence": 82,
          "component": "Presentation Conversion",
          "source": "one_call",
          "confidence": 1.0,
          "text": "We take in consideration the configuration for enabling and disabling SWF, SVG and PNG conversion."
        },
        {
          "sentence": 83,
          "component": "Presentation Conversion",
          "source": "one_call",
          "confidence": 1.0,
          "text": "Then below the SVG conversion flow."
        },
        {
          "sentence": 84,
          "component": "Presentation Conversion",
          "source": "one_call",
          "confidence": 1.0,
          "text": "It covers the conversion fallback."
        },
        {
          "sentence": 85,
          "component": "Presentation Conversion",
          "source": "one_call",
          "confidence": 1.0,
          "text": "Sometimes we detect that the generated SVG file is heavy to load by the browser, we use the fallback to put a rasterized"
        }
      ],
